The app will be built with the latest dotnet version
It will be an dotnet api with a domain slice architecture
In its slice a domain will be developed
One api project will be used, and slice will be separated on directories
For each slice a minimal api will be used and for each operation of the slice a handler will be creted, similar to cqrs pattern but with no mediator,commands and queries, just a handler with his interface
Each slice will contain 
    - a <domain>minimalapi.cs file, containing the endpoints
    - a core directory containing the db entities of the domain
    - An application directory containing sub directories for handlers and their models
    - A service directory, if necessary for services operating specific works specific to this domain
    - An infrustructure directory containing IO related operation, ie db migrations
    - In case 2 domains should communicate, an ExternalInterface directory will be added containing a public interface for the other domain, and a private implementation of it